# Line endings are LF everywhere, including on Windows checkouts.
#
# Two files in this repository are generated and then checked, by tests
# that regenerate them and compare against what is on disk -- that is how
# `aria.rs` and `tailwind_variants.rs` are kept honest about the ARIA
# specification and Tailwind's own variant list.
#
# GitHub's Windows runners set `core.autocrlf=true`, so a checkout there
# rewrote every LF to CRLF while the generators kept writing LF. The
# comparison then failed on every line of both files, for a difference
# that exists only in the checkout. It passed on Linux, on macOS, and on
# the Windows machine this is developed on, because none of those rewrite
# anything -- the one configuration that does is the one nobody was
# looking at.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binary files and leave them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
